    2. Choose 2-5 plus centers (rows 1-10, cols 1-10). Group them into 1-3
       clusters; within a cluster, centers are L1 dist 1-2 apart; between
       clusters, >=5 apart.
    3. Mark each center and its 4 arms as GREEN (the output state).
    4. Scatter additional BLACK pixels randomly across remaining TEAL cells
       until ~40-52% of the grid is BLACK+GREEN. Ensure no accidental new
       plus centers form (check each newly placed black pixel and its neighbors).
    5. Output grid = current grid. Input grid = copy with all GREEN replaced
       by BLACK.
